course: dictionary
lesson: 582
title: Autocorrect is a helper, not a proofreader
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Autocorrect is a tool in phones and computers that changes words it thinks are spelled wrong while you type. It helps you spell, but it only looks at single words, not at what your sentence means.
explain: «The dog bark at the mail man» passes a spelling check, because every word is a real word. Yet bark should be barked, and a reader stumbles over it. Autocorrect cannot see that mistake.
explain: So autocorrect is a helper, not an editor. Always read your writing back yourself before you send it, and ask: does this say what I mean?
fact: Autocorrect is a noun: a tool in phones and computers that changes words it thinks are wrong.
fact: As a verb, autocorrect means to change a word in this way, so a phone might autocorrect «teh» to «the».
fact: Autocorrect is not always right, so it can make funny or embarrassing mistakes.
fact: People say «turn off autocorrect» to stop it changing their words, or «blame autocorrect» when a mistake gets through.
fact: Autocorrect checks spelling, but it does not check whether your sentence makes sense.
exercise: What is autocorrect? | A game where you race to type the fastest | A paper dictionary | A keyboard with extra letters | *A tool in phones and computers that changes words it thinks are spelled wrong
exercise: In «The dog bark at the mail man», why does autocorrect miss the mistake? | The sentence is too long | The sentence is a question | The words are all in capital letters | *Every word is a real word, so it looks correct
exercise: Which word means to change a word in this way? | autograph | autumn | author | *autocorrect
test: Why should you read your writing back after autocorrect has helped? | *Autocorrect checks spelling, not whether the meaning is right | Autocorrect only works at night | Reading back makes the phone faster | Autocorrect writes your whole story for you
test: What does the phrase «turn off autocorrect» mean? | Delete all your messages | Switch the keyboard to a new language | Make the phone louder | *Stop the tool from changing your words
exam: Which is the best way to use autocorrect? | Let a friend type every word for you | Trust it completely and never check your work | *Use it as a helper, then read your work back yourself to check the meaning | Turn it on only for poems
